UPDATE public.legal_documents SET
  title = $P$Privacy Policy$P$,
  content = $P$<p><strong>Effective date:</strong> 5 March 2026 · <strong>Version:</strong> 1.0</p>

<h2>1. Summary</h2>
<p>Anacan never sells your health data, never uses it for advertising, and processes it only with your explicit consent. This Policy applies to the anacan.az website, the Anacan mobile app (iOS and Android) and related services (hereinafter the "Service").</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Our commitment</th><th>What it means</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Health data is not sold</td><td>We do not sell or rent pregnancy, cycle, symptom or child health data to anyone, and we do not pass it on to advertising networks, insurance companies or employers.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Explicit consent</td><td>Health data is processed only with your separate, explicit consent; you can withdraw your consent at any time.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Data minimisation</td><td>We collect only what is necessary for a feature to work.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Restricted staff access</td><td>Our staff may see your health data only at your request, with your consent, for a limited time and with logging.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Strong protection</td><td>TLS 1.2+ encryption in transit and AES-256 encryption at rest.</td></tr>
<tr><td>You are in full control</td><td>You can download and correct your data in the app and delete it completely using the delete account button.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Global standard</td><td>The app is distributed in all countries where the App Store and Google Play are available; we apply the strictest standard — the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) — as the baseline for all users. Where local law requires more protection, local law prevails (Section 13).</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Anacan is not a medical device and does not replace a doctor's advice. The rules for using the Service are set out in the separate Terms of Use.</p>

<h2>2. Who we are and to whom this Policy applies</h2>
<p>The controller of your data (within the meaning of Article 4(7) GDPR) is "ANACAN" LLC, registered in the Republic of Azerbaijan (TIN 1407578211; hereinafter "Anacan", "we").</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Controller</td><td>"ANACAN" LLC, TIN 1407578211, 150 Shamil Azizbeyov St., Baku, Azerbaijan</td></tr>
<tr><td>Data Protection Officer (DPO)</td><td>Jamil Sultanli, privacy@anacan.az</td></tr>
<tr><td>EU representative (Art. 27 GDPR)</td><td>Appointment in progress; will be listed here once appointed. Currently: privacy@anacan.az</td></tr>
<tr><td>UK representative (Art. 27 UK GDPR)</td><td>Appointment in progress; will be listed here once appointed. Currently: privacy@anacan.az</td></tr>
<tr><td>Other local representatives</td><td>Appointed where required by local law and listed here</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Users in the EU and the United Kingdom may contact our representative instead of, or in addition to, us on any data protection matter (until a representative is appointed, please write to privacy@anacan.az).</p>
<h3>What this Policy covers</h3>
<ul>
<li>The anacan.az website and its subdomains</li>
<li>The Anacan mobile app (App Store, Google Play and other app stores)</li>
<li>Newsletters, push notifications, customer support, surveys and campaigns</li>
<li>The Anacan.AI assistant and community (forum) features</li>
<li>Cookies and similar technologies used on the website and in the app</li>
</ul>
<h3>What it does not cover</h3>
<ul>
<li>Third-party websites and services opened via links from the Service (their own policies apply)</li>
<li>Data of Anacan employees and job applicants (separate internal policy)</li>
<li>Data processed by Apple, Google and payment services themselves as independent controllers</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. What data we collect</h2>
<p>We obtain data in three ways: you provide it, it is generated automatically when you use the Service, and in limited cases we receive it from partners (e.g. subscription status from the app store).</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Examples</th><th>Source</th><th>Mandatory?</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Account data</td><td>Name (or nickname), e-mail, password hash, sign-in method (Apple, Google), language, country</td><td>You</td><td>Yes, to create an account</td></tr>
<tr><td>Profile data</td><td>Life stage (planning, pregnancy, parenthood)</td><td>You</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>Health data (special category)</td><td>Pregnancy week, estimated due date, menstrual cycle, ovulation, symptoms, mood, weight, blood pressure, test results, medications, fetal movements, contractions, IVF, pregnancy loss, type of delivery</td><td>You</td><td>No — only with explicit consent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Data about the child</td><td>Name (optional), date of birth, sex, height, weight, feeding, sleep, vaccinations, developmental milestones, photos</td><td>You (the parent)</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>AI assistant</td><td>Questions you write to Anacan.AI and the answers</td><td>You</td><td>No — only with consent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Community content</td><td>Forum posts, comments, likes</td><td>You</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>Payment data</td><td>Subscription type, purchase date, country, transaction ID. We do not see or store your card number — payments are processed by Apple, Google or, on the website, Epoint (bank payment page)</td><td>App store, payment provider</td><td>Yes, for paid features</td></tr>
<tr><td>Device and technical data</td><td>Device model, operating system, app version, language, time zone, IP address, error logs, push token</td><td>Automatic</td><td>Yes, for technical operation</td></tr>
<tr><td>Usage data</td><td>Screens opened, features used, session duration (without health content)</td><td>Automatic</td><td>With analytics consent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Approximate location</td><td>Country and city based on IP</td><td>Automatic</td><td>Yes (for language, law and content)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Precise location</td><td>GPS (e.g. map of nearby maternity hospitals and pharmacies)</td><td>Device</td><td>No — only with permission, not stored</td></tr>
<tr><td>Contact and support</td><td>Requests, correspondence, feedback</td><td>You</td><td>No</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Special notes on sensitive data</h3>
<ul>
<li>Under Article 9 GDPR, health data is a "special category" of data and is stored at the highest level of protection.</li>
<li>Menstrual cycle, pregnancy and pregnancy loss data may carry legal risk in some countries. We therefore disclose such data only where required by law and only after it has passed the review described in Section 7.4.</li>
<li>We do not collect biometric data, facial recognition data, genetic data, or data about race, religion, political opinions or sex life. The Face ID / fingerprint check for the app lock is performed on your device and is not transmitted to us. Please do not enter such information in free-text fields.</li>
<li>We access your photo gallery, camera and microphone only at the moment you open the relevant feature and only with your permission.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
<p>Every processing operation is based on one of the legal bases in Article 6 GDPR and, for health data, additionally on Article 9(2)(a) (explicit consent). We do not rely on "legitimate interest" for health data.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Data categories</th><th>Legal basis</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Creating and managing the account</td><td>Account, device</td><td>Performance of a contract — Art. 6(1)(b)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Personal pregnancy, cycle and baby calendars, reminders, tracking tools</td><td>Health, child</td><td>Explicit consent — Art. 9(2)(a) and Art. 6(1)(a)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Personalising content by pregnancy week or child's age</td><td>Health, child</td><td>Explicit consent — Art. 9(2)(a)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Anacan.AI assistant</td><td>Your questions, the context you select</td><td>Explicit consent — Art. 9(2)(a) and Art. 6(1)(a)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Subscriptions and payments</td><td>Payment, account</td><td>Contract — Art. 6(1)(b); legal obligation for tax records — Art. 6(1)(c)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Technical support and responding to requests</td><td>Account, contact; health only with your consent</td><td>Contract — Art. 6(1)(b); Art. 9(2)(a) for health</td></tr>
<tr><td>Security, fraud prevention, abuse detection</td><td>Device, technical, account</td><td>Legitimate interest — Art. 6(1)(f)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bug fixing and stability</td><td>Device, technical</td><td>Legitimate interest — Art. 6(1)(f)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Analytics to improve the product</td><td>Usage (without health content)</td><td>Consent — Art. 6(1)(a)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Advertising and ad measurement in the free version</td><td>Advertising identifier, device (without health content)</td><td>Consent for personalised advertising and measurement — Art. 6(1)(a); legitimate interest for non-personalised advertising — Art. 6(1)(f)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Anonymised, aggregated statistics</td><td>Anonymous data</td><td>Anonymous data is not personal data; the original consent for the anonymisation process itself</td></tr>
<tr><td>Service notices (security, changes to terms)</td><td>Account</td><td>Contract — Art. 6(1)(b); legal obligation — Art. 6(1)(c)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Marketing e-mails and push notifications</td><td>Account, contact</td><td>Consent — Art. 6(1)(a); opt out at any time</td></tr>
<tr><td>Community moderation and tackling illegal content</td><td>Community content</td><td>Legitimate interest — Art. 6(1)(f); legal obligation under the EU Digital Services Act — Art. 6(1)(c)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Defending legal claims, lawful requests</td><td>To the extent necessary</td><td>Legal obligation — Art. 6(1)(c); Art. 9(2)(f)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Protecting vital interests in a medical emergency (exceptional case)</td><td>Minimum necessary</td><td>Vital interest — Art. 6(1)(d), Art. 9(2)(c)</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>How we obtain explicit consent</h3>
<ul>
<li>Consent is obtained on a separate screen, with options that are not pre-ticked, explaining in plain language which data will be used and for what purpose.</li>
<li>Consent is separated by purpose (health data, AI assistant, marketing, analytics). Consent to one does not mean consent to another.</li>
<li>Analytics and marketing consent is not a condition for using the Service.</li>
<li>The date, version and type of consent are recorded as evidence.</li>
<li>Withdrawing consent: in the app, Profile → Privacy → Consents. Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of prior processing. When you withdraw health consent, you can request deletion of the related data; we carry out your request within 30 days and, if you wish, let you export it first.</li>
</ul>
<h3>About legitimate interest</h3>
<p>We rely on legitimate interest only for security, technical stability, non-personalised advertising and moderation. A legitimate interest assessment (LIA) has been carried out and documented for each of these; we provide a short summary on request. You may object to this processing under Article 21 GDPR.</p>

<h2>5. Cookies, SDKs, analytics and advertising</h2>
<p>Non-essential cookies and SDKs are activated only after you give your consent; health data is never passed to any advertising or analytics SDK.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Consent required?</th><th>Example tools</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Essential</td><td>Sign-in, security, language selection, remembering consent choices, cart</td><td>No</td><td>Our own cookies and local storage (localStorage), Google Cloud</td></tr>
<tr><td>Analytics</td><td>Understanding which sections are used</td><td>Yes</td><td>Google Analytics 4 on the website; Google Analytics for Firebase in the app</td></tr>
<tr><td>Advertising (free version of the app only)</td><td>Showing ads and measuring ad performance</td><td>Yes, for personalised advertising and measurement</td><td>Google AdMob; Meta App Events (only with "Ad measurement" consent)</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Third-party SDKs we use in the app: Google Analytics for Firebase, Firebase Cloud Messaging, Customer.io, RevenueCat, Google AdMob and Meta App Events. Advertising and analytics SDKs operate only in line with your choices; Premium subscribers are not shown ads.</p>
<h3>Managing consent</h3>
<ul>
<li>On your first visit to the website a cookie banner is shown: the "Accept" and "Essential only" buttons are the same size and at the same level.</li>
<li>You can change your choice at any time via the "Cookie settings" link at the bottom of the website or in the app under Profile → Privacy.</li>
<li>Consent is requested again every 6 months; if you decline, we remember that choice and do not ask again on every visit.</li>
<li>We recognise your browser's "Global Privacy Control" (GPC) signal and treat it as a rejection of non-essential cookies and as an opt-out of "sale/sharing".</li>
<li>On iOS we do not collect the advertising identifier (IDFA) without Apple's "App Tracking Transparency" permission. In the app, consent for personalised advertising is requested via Google's consent dialog.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Our advertising rules</h3>
<ul>
<li>Health data, pregnancy or cycle status, and sensitive events such as pregnancy loss are not passed to advertising networks, social media pixels or data brokers — not even as "events".</li>
<li>Ads shown in the free version are not based on your personal health profile; personalised ads are shown only with your consent.</li>
<li>We send Anacan's own product recommendations (e.g. an offer matched to your pregnancy week) by push or e-mail only if you have given separate marketing consent.</li>
<li>Personalised ads are not shown to users we know to be under 18.</li>
<li>When a pregnancy loss is recorded, all pregnancy- and baby-related marketing notifications are stopped immediately.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Age limit and data about children</h2>
<p>The minimum age for independent use of Anacan is 16; if the law of your country requires a higher age (the digital age of consent), that age applies.</p>
<h3>Age limit</h3>
<ul>
<li>During registration we ask you to confirm that you are over 16; users who do not confirm cannot use the account.</li>
<li>We do not knowingly collect data from children under 13 (including as required by COPPA in the US).</li>
<li>For users who are above the minimum age but under 18, no personalised advertising or marketing profile is created, and content is presented in an age-appropriate way.</li>
<li>If we learn that a person below the minimum age has created an account, we delete the account and data as soon as possible. Please report such cases to privacy@anacan.az.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Child data entered by a parent</h3>
<p>In features such as the baby diary, development calendar and vaccination reminders, data about your child is entered by you — the parent or legal guardian.</p>
<ul>
<li>By entering this data you confirm that you are the child's parent or legal guardian and that you have the right to give consent on the child's behalf.</li>
<li>Child data is stored at the same (highest) level of protection as your health data and is not used for any advertising or profiling.</li>
<li>Your child's photos are stored privately in your account only; they are not visible to anyone unless you yourself share them in the community. We recommend that you take care when sharing a child's photo in the community.</li>
<li>You can delete a child profile separately at any time.</li>
<li>If two parents use a shared profile (the "Partner invitation" feature), the inviting person chooses which data is shared and can stop sharing at any time.</li>
</ul>

<h2>7. Who we share data with</h2>
<p>We share your data only in the cases below, on the basis of a written contract and to the minimum extent necessary. We never sell your personal data.</p>
<h3>7.1. Processors (services acting on our behalf)</h3>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Receives health data?</th><th>Provider</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Cloud hosting and database</td><td>Operation of the Service</td><td>Yes, in encrypted form</td><td>Google Cloud (Google LLC), Belgium</td></tr>
<tr><td>E-mail and push notification delivery</td><td>Notifications</td><td>No (texts are written neutrally)</td><td>Customer.io, Inc.; Firebase Cloud Messaging (Google LLC)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Support</td><td>Requests</td><td>Only if you write it</td><td>Google Workspace (Google LLC)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Analytics</td><td>Product improvement</td><td>No</td><td>Google Analytics, Firebase (Google LLC)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Subscription management</td><td>Verification of store purchases</td><td>No</td><td>RevenueCat, Inc.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Card payments on the website</td><td>Payments for subscriptions, books and cakes</td><td>No</td><td>Epoint (bank payment page)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Advertising (free version)</td><td>Showing and measuring ads</td><td>No</td><td>Google AdMob (Google LLC); Meta Platforms (only with "Ad measurement" consent)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Security and CDN</td><td>Protection against attacks</td><td>No</td><td>Google Cloud (Google LLC)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Enterprise AI service</td><td>Anacan.AI assistant (Section 12)</td><td>Only with your consent; the provider does not use the data to train its own models</td><td>Google Gemini, Vertex AI (Google LLC)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Translation of community posts</td><td>Displaying posts in other languages</td><td>Only if you write it in a post yourself</td><td>Anthropic, PBC; Microsoft Azure OpenAI</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>A data processing agreement (DPA) in accordance with Article 28 GDPR is concluded with each processor. Suppliers that process health data undergo a security review in advance. When we add a new processor, we update this table at least 15 days in advance.</p>
<h3>7.2. Independent parties</h3>
<ul>
<li>Apple, Google and payment providers — for processing payments; they are independent controllers acting under their own policies.</li>
<li>Exports by you — when you yourself send data to your doctor or to services such as Apple Health / Health Connect.</li>
<li>Professional advisers — lawyers, auditors (bound by confidentiality obligations).</li>
<li>Merger or sale of the company — in that case the new owner will have to accept the obligations in this Policy; we will notify you in advance, and health data may not be used for a different purpose without new consent.</li>
</ul>
<h3>7.3. What we never do</h3>
<ul>
<li>Pass data to data brokers, insurance companies, credit institutions or employers.</li>
<li>Share health data for advertising or "cross-context behavioral advertising" purposes.</li>
<li>Share identifiable data for scientific research without your separate consent.</li>
</ul>
<h3>7.4. Requests from public authorities</h3>
<p>Requests from law enforcement and other public authorities are handled only by our legal team and the DPO.</p>
<ul>
<li>Data is disclosed only in the manner prescribed by law, on the basis of an official written request and to the minimum extent.</li>
<li>We verify the lawfulness of each request and challenge overly broad or unfounded requests.</li>
<li>We pay particular attention to requests concerning reproductive health data (cycle, pregnancy, pregnancy loss) and use all available legal remedies.</li>
<li>Unless prohibited by law, we inform you about the request.</li>
<li>Every request is recorded in a register; we publish the number of requests in an annual transparency report.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. International transfers</h2>
<p>Your data is stored on Google Cloud infrastructure, on servers located in the European Union (Belgium); transfers outside your country take place only under one of the legal mechanisms below and with supplementary safeguards.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Transfer direction</th><th>Legal mechanism</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>EU/EEA → country with an adequacy decision (e.g. UK, Switzerland, Japan, Canada)</td><td>European Commission adequacy decision — Art. 45 GDPR</td></tr>
<tr><td>EU/EEA → USA</td><td>If the provider is certified under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework — Art. 45; otherwise Standard Contractual Clauses</td></tr>
<tr><td>EU/EEA → other countries, including Azerbaijan</td><td>European Commission Standard Contractual Clauses (SCC, 2021) — Art. 46(2)(c) and a transfer impact assessment (TIA)</td></tr>
<tr><td>UK → other countries</td><td>UK International Data Transfer Agreement (IDTA) or the UK Addendum to the SCC</td></tr>
<tr><td>Türkiye → abroad</td><td>Standard contract under KVKK; notification to the Personal Data Protection Authority within 5 business days after the contract is signed</td></tr>
<tr><td>Other countries</td><td>Mechanism recognised by that country's law (standard contract, consent, etc.) — Section 13</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Supplementary safeguards</h3>
<ul>
<li>Encryption in transit and at rest; access to encryption keys is strictly limited.</li>
<li>Where possible, data is pseudonymised before transfer.</li>
<li>Requests from foreign public authorities are reviewed and challenged in accordance with Section 7.4.</li>
<li>You can obtain a copy of the Standard Contractual Clauses by sending a request to privacy@anacan.az (parts containing trade secrets may be redacted).</li>
</ul>

<h2>9. Retention periods</h2>
<p>We keep data only for as long as necessary for the purpose; when an account is deleted, health data is deleted from active systems within 30 days and from backups within 90 days.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Retention period</th><th>Afterwards</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Account data</td><td>While the account is active</td><td>Deleted within 30 days after the deletion request</td></tr>
<tr><td>Health and child data</td><td>While the account is active and consent remains in effect</td><td>Deleted within 30 days when the account is deleted or when you withdraw consent and request deletion</td></tr>
<tr><td>Backups</td><td>Up to 90 days</td><td>Automatically overwritten; deleted data is deleted again upon restoration</td></tr>
<tr><td>Inactive account</td><td>24 months of inactivity</td><td>The account is deleted 30 days after a warning</td></tr>
<tr><td>AI chat history</td><td>While the account is active; you can delete it at any time</td><td>Deleted when the account is deleted</td></tr>
<tr><td>Community posts</td><td>Until you delete them</td><td>Deleted when the account is deleted</td></tr>
<tr><td>Payment records</td><td>The period required by Azerbaijani tax and accounting legislation</td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
<tr><td>Support requests</td><td>2 years after closure</td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
<tr><td>Technical and security logs</td><td>Up to 90 days; for incident investigation, not exceeding 12 months</td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
<tr><td>Analytics data</td><td>14 months</td><td>Aggregated or deleted</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consent records</td><td>3 years after consent is withdrawn (as evidence)</td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
<tr><td>Register of public authority requests</td><td>5 years</td><td>Deleted</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Once the period expires, data is deleted or irreversibly anonymised. If a legal dispute or lawful request is ongoing, the relevant data is kept in blocked form only until that matter is concluded.</p>

<h2>10. Security and incidents</h2>
<p>We protect health data as the highest risk category and, in the event of a data breach, we notify you without waiting.</p>
<h3>Technical and organisational measures</h3>
<ul>
<li>Encryption: TLS 1.2+ in transit, AES-256 at rest (server disks and backups); encryption keys are held by Google Cloud's managed key service.</li>
<li>Access control: principle of least privilege, multi-factor authentication for staff; access to health data is logged and regularly reviewed.</li>
<li>Protecting your account: option to lock the app with a PIN, Face ID or fingerprint; e-mail verification.</li>
<li>Secure development: code review, vulnerability scanning of dependencies, an independent penetration test at least once a year.</li>
<li>Staff: confidentiality undertakings are signed and annual data protection training is completed.</li>
<li>Assessment: a data protection impact assessment (DPIA) is carried out for every new feature that processes health data — Art. 35 GDPR.</li>
</ul>
<h3>If a data breach occurs</h3>
<ol>
<li>We immediately contain the incident, investigate its cause and record it.</li>
<li>If there is a risk, we notify the supervisory authority within 72 hours of becoming aware of it (Art. 33 GDPR); in other countries we comply with the deadline set by local law.</li>
<li>If the breach poses a high risk to your rights and freedoms, we inform you without undue delay of what happened, which data was affected and how you can protect yourself (Art. 34 GDPR).</li>
<li>If health data is affected, we inform the affected users regardless of the risk level.</li>
</ol>
<p>If you have found a vulnerability, please write to security@anacan.az. We do not bring legal claims over vulnerabilities reported in good faith.</p>

<h2>11. Your rights and how to exercise them</h2>
<p>Wherever you live, we guarantee all users the rights below; we respond to requests free of charge and within 1 month.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Right</th><th>What it means</th><th>How to exercise it</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Access (Art. 15)</td><td>Learn which of your data we process and why, and receive a copy</td><td>Profile → Settings → Data export; privacy@anacan.az</td></tr>
<tr><td>Rectification (Art. 16)</td><td>Correct inaccurate or incomplete data</td><td>Edit directly in the app or contact support</td></tr>
<tr><td>Erasure (Art. 17)</td><td>Complete deletion of your data or account</td><td>Profile → Settings → Privacy &amp; Data → Delete account; you can also delete individual entries and the child profile separately</td></tr>
<tr><td>Restriction of processing (Art. 18)</td><td>Suspend the use of data until a dispute is resolved</td><td>privacy@anacan.az</td></tr>
<tr><td>Portability (Art. 20)</td><td>Receive data in a machine-readable format (JSON) or transfer it to another service</td><td>Profile → Settings → Data export</td></tr>
<tr><td>Objection (Art. 21)</td><td>Object to processing based on legitimate interest and to direct marketing</td><td>Profile → Privacy → Consents; privacy@anacan.az</td></tr>
<tr><td>Withdrawal of consent (Art. 7(3))</td><td>Revoke any consent given at any time</td><td>Profile → Privacy → Consents</td></tr>
<tr><td>Not to be subject to automated decisions (Art. 22)</td><td>Not to be subject to decisions with legal effects based solely on automated processing</td><td>Section 12</td></tr>
<tr><td>Complaint (Art. 77)</td><td>Lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority</td><td>Section 14</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>How requests are handled</h3>
<ul>
<li>You can submit a request from the app or by writing to privacy@anacan.az.</li>
<li>We verify your identity by sign-in to your account or via your registered e-mail; we do not ask for more documents than necessary.</li>
<li>The response time is 1 month; for complex requests it may be extended by 2 months, with the reason explained. Where local law requires a shorter period, that period applies (Section 13).</li>
<li>An authorised representative may submit a request on your behalf with a written power of attorney.</li>
<li>If we refuse a request, we inform you in writing of the reason and of your right to complain.</li>
<li>Exercising your rights does not change your level of service or price.</li>
</ul>

<h2>12. AI features and automated decisions</h2>
<p>Anacan does not make fully automated decisions about you that produce legal or similarly significant effects; the AI assistant provides only informational answers and does not make diagnoses.</p>
<h3>Anacan.AI assistant</h3>
<ul>
<li>The AI assistant is an optional feature; separate consent is requested on first use. If you do not consent, the rest of the Service works fully.</li>
<li>What you write to the assistant and the context used to make the answer more accurate (e.g. pregnancy week) are transmitted to Google's Gemini service (Section 7.1). Google does not use this data to train its own models and retains it only for the limited period provided for in the contract terms, to prevent abuse.</li>
<li>You can view and delete your chat history in the app.</li>
<li>We do not use your chats to train our own AI models.</li>
<li>AI answers may be wrong. If urgent symptoms are mentioned (bleeding, severe pain, reduced fetal movements, etc.), the assistant advises you to contact a doctor or emergency services immediately.</li>
<li>In the EU this feature operates in accordance with the transparency requirements of the EU AI Act: it is clearly indicated that you are interacting with AI.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Personalisation and profiling</h3>
<p>Selecting content by pregnancy week or child's age is done using simple rules based on the stage information you enter and has no legal effect on you. No profile is created on the basis of health data for decisions such as credit, insurance or employment.</p>
<h3>Community</h3>
<p>What you write in the forum is visible to other users. We recommend posting under a nickname and not sharing recognisable photos of your face or your child, or information such as your address and phone number. Automatic filters are used in moderation, but the final decision is made by a moderator; you can appeal a decision.</p>

