<h2>7. AI assistant (Anacan.AI)</h2>
<p>The AI assistant is an artificial intelligence system and can make mistakes; its responses are general information and do not replace a doctor's consultation.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Transparency.</strong> When chatting with the AI assistant, it is clearly indicated that you are interacting with artificial intelligence and not a human (transparency requirements of the EU AI Act).</li>
<li><strong>Consent.</strong> The assistant is optional, and separate consent is requested on first use. If you do not consent, the other parts of the Service work fully. You can withdraw consent under Profile → Privacy → Consents.</li>
<li><strong>Nature of responses.</strong> Responses are generated automatically, may be incomplete, outdated or incorrect, and are not medically reviewed. Do not treat them as medical advice, a diagnosis or a treatment prescription.</li>
<li><strong>Emergencies.</strong> When the assistant recognises emergency signs, it directs you to a doctor or emergency services, but there is no guarantee that it will recognise every emergency. If emergency signs are present, follow Section 3.4.</li>
<li><strong>Prohibited use.</strong> It is prohibited to use the assistant for unlawful or harmful purposes, to collect information about another person without authorisation, to deceive the system or to circumvent its restrictions.</li>
<li><strong>Data.</strong> Your conversations are transmitted to the AI provider named in the Privacy Policy; neither we nor the provider use them to train models. When you delete your account, your conversations are also deleted.</li>
<li><strong>Limits.</strong> The free version may have a message limit; limits are shown in the app.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. User Content, community and moderation</h2>
<p>What you share in the community remains yours; we receive only the limited licence needed to operate the Service, and we take moderation decisions transparently in accordance with the EU Digital Services Act (DSA).</p>

<h3>8.1. Rights in content and licence</h3>
<ul>
<li>You retain the rights in your User Content.</li>
<li>By sharing, you grant Anacan a non-exclusive, royalty-free, non-transferable, worldwide licence to store, display and technically reformat (e.g. resize an image) that content within the Service and to deliver it to the audience you choose.</li>
<li>The licence ends when you delete the content or close your account; deletion from technical backups occurs within the period stated in the Privacy Policy. Parts quoted in other users' replies may remain.</li>
<li>We use your content outside the Service (e.g. in advertising or on social media) only with your separate, explicit consent.</li>
<li>You are responsible for the content you share and for having the right to share it.</li>
</ul>

<h3>8.2. Community Guidelines</h3>
<p>The following are prohibited in the community:</p>
<ul>
<li>Dangerous medical information: unproven "treatments", false anti-vaccine claims, sale or exchange of prescription medicines, methods of unlawful termination of pregnancy</li>
<li>Content promoting self-harm, suicide or eating disorders</li>
<li>Insults, threats, hate speech, harassment, and shaming or condemning other parents</li>
<li>Sharing another person's personal or health information, including photos of children, without their consent</li>
<li>Any content that sexually exploits children or is of a sexual nature involving children (removed immediately and reported to the competent authorities)</li>
<li>Spam, covert advertising, affiliate links, fake reviews, unauthorised sale of goods and services</li>
<li>Impersonating another person or professional (e.g. presenting oneself as a doctor without being one)</li>
<li>Content that infringes intellectual property rights</li>
</ul>

<h3>8.3. Notice of illegal content</h3>
<ul>
<li>You can report illegal content or content that breaches the rules using the "Report" button next to the post or by writing to dsa@anacan.az. No account is required to report by e-mail.</li>
<li>A notice should include the location of the content (link), an explanation of why you consider it illegal, your name and e-mail address (except for notices concerning child sexual abuse) and a statement confirming that the information is accurate.</li>
<li>We confirm receipt of the notice, review it in a timely, objective and diligent manner, and inform you of our decision.</li>
</ul>

<h3>8.4. Moderation decisions and statement of reasons</h3>
<ul>
<li>Moderation is carried out by a combination of automated tools (detection of spam and dangerous keywords) and human moderators. Serious decisions such as account termination are taken by a human.</li>
<li>If we remove your content, restrict its visibility, or suspend or terminate your account, we send you a statement of reasons: what action was taken, on which facts and rules it was based, whether automated means were used, and what redress options are available to you.</li>
</ul>

<h3>8.5. Complaints and dispute resolution</h3>
