<h3>6.1. Purchase channels</h3>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Channel</th><th>Seller and payment</th><th>Cancellation and refund</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>iOS app (App Store)</td><td>Apple; payment from your Apple account</td><td>Apple ID settings → Subscriptions; refunds under Apple's rules (reportaproblem.apple.com)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Android app (Google Play)</td><td>Google; payment from your Google account</td><td>Google Play → Payments &amp; subscriptions; refunds under Google's rules</td></tr>
<tr><td>anacan.az website and in-app card payment</td><td>Anacan; payment via a certified payment provider (Epoint)</td><td>"Cancel" on the anacan.az/premium/hesab page; refunds by Anacan</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>We do not store your bank card details; they are processed by the Platform or the payment provider.</p>

<h3>6.2. Prices and taxes</h3>
<ul>
<li>The price, subscription period, renewal terms and trial period are clearly shown on the purchase screen before payment.</li>
<li>Prices are shown in local currency and, where required by law, including VAT.</li>
<li>Anacan is not responsible for currency conversion or additional fees charged by your bank.</li>
</ul>

<h3>6.3. Automatic renewal and cancellation</h3>
<ul>
<li>Unless cancelled at least 24 hours before the end of the current period, the subscription automatically renews for the same term and at the same price.</li>
<li>Where required by local law, we send a reminder before an annual subscription renews.</li>
<li>You may cancel the subscription at any time, through the channel where you purchased it, as easily as you subscribed. After cancellation, access continues until the end of the paid period.</li>
<li>Deleting the app does not cancel the subscription.</li>
<li>Except where required by law, no partial refunds are given for unused periods.</li>
</ul>

<h3>6.4. Free trial</h3>
<ul>
<li>The length of the trial and the price after it ends are shown before the trial begins.</li>
<li>Unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the trial ends, the paid subscription begins.</li>
<li>A free trial is granted once per user.</li>
</ul>

<h3>6.5. Price changes</h3>
<ul>
<li>We give at least 30 days' notice of any increase in the subscription price.</li>
<li>Where the law or Platform rules so require, the new price applies only with your consent; if you do not consent, the subscription ends at the end of the current period.</li>
<li>The new price takes effect only from the next renewal period.</li>
</ul>

<h3>6.6. Right of withdrawal (EU, EEA, United Kingdom, Türkiye)</h3>
<p>As a consumer residing in these countries, you have the right to withdraw from the contract without giving any reason within 14 days of the day the contract is concluded (for physical goods, from the day you receive the goods).</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>How to exercise it:</strong> (a) by sending the withdrawal form in the Annex or any other clear statement to support@anacan.az; (b) for a subscription purchased on the App Store or Google Play, through that Platform's refund process. We confirm receipt of your withdrawal statement by e-mail.</li>
<li><strong>Premium subscription (digital service):</strong> if you expressly requested that the service begin immediately during the withdrawal period, upon withdrawal only an amount proportionate to the period used up to withdrawal may be charged, and the remainder is refunded.</li>
<li><strong>Digital content (e.g. a PDF book):</strong> if supply begins before the withdrawal period expires, before purchase you are asked (i) to give express consent to immediate supply and (ii) to acknowledge that you thereby lose your right of withdrawal. Without this acknowledgement, your right of withdrawal remains.</li>
<li><strong>Physical goods:</strong> return the goods within 14 days of your withdrawal statement; the cost of return is borne by you unless otherwise stated at the time of purchase. Perishable goods (e.g. cakes), goods made to order or personalised, and sealed hygiene goods that have been unsealed fall within the statutory exceptions.</li>
<li><strong>Refund:</strong> we refund no later than 14 days after receiving your withdrawal statement, using the payment method you used, without any additional charge. For physical goods, we may withhold the refund until we have received the goods back or you have provided proof of having sent them.</li>
</ul>

<h3>6.7. Lack of conformity and legal guarantee</h3>
<p>Digital content and services, as well as physical goods, must conform to the contract. In the EU and the United Kingdom, if the Service does not work or does not match its description, you have statutory rights: to have it brought into conformity (repair), to a price reduction, or to terminate the contract and receive a refund. The legal guarantee period for physical goods in the EU is at least 2 years. These rights are independent of any voluntary warranties and cannot be restricted.</p>

<h3>6.8. United States and other countries</h3>
<ul>
<li>In the US, the disclosures required by state laws for automatically renewing subscriptions (e.g. California's Automatic Renewal Law) are provided on the purchase screen, and online cancellation is made available.</li>
<li>In other countries, if local consumer laws grant you additional withdrawal or refund rights, those rights apply.</li>
</ul>

<h3>6.9. Failed payments and payment disputes</h3>
<ul>
<li>If a renewal payment fails, access may be retained during the Platform's grace period; if payment is not completed, Premium is suspended, while free features and your data remain.</li>
<li>If you have a payment issue, we ask that you write to support@anacan.az before contacting your bank; we usually resolve the matter more quickly. This does not restrict your right to contact your bank.</li>
</ul>

<h2>7. AI assistant (Anacan.AI)</h2>
<p>The AI assistant is an artificial intelligence system and can make mistakes; its responses are general information and do not replace a doctor's consultation.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Transparency.</strong> When chatting with the AI assistant, it is clearly indicated that you are interacting with artificial intelligence and not a human (transparency requirements of the EU AI Act).</li>
<li><strong>Consent.</strong> The assistant is optional, and separate consent is requested on first use. If you do not consent, the other parts of the Service work fully. You can withdraw consent under Profile → Privacy → Consents.</li>
<li><strong>Nature of responses.</strong> Responses are generated automatically, may be incomplete, outdated or incorrect, and are not medically reviewed. Do not treat them as medical advice, a diagnosis or a treatment prescription.</li>
<li><strong>Emergencies.</strong> When the assistant recognises emergency signs, it directs you to a doctor or emergency services, but there is no guarantee that it will recognise every emergency. If emergency signs are present, follow Section 3.4.</li>
<li><strong>Prohibited use.</strong> It is prohibited to use the assistant for unlawful or harmful purposes, to collect information about another person without authorisation, to deceive the system or to circumvent its restrictions.</li>
<li><strong>Data.</strong> Your conversations are transmitted to the AI provider named in the Privacy Policy; neither we nor the provider use them to train models. When you delete your account, your conversations are also deleted.</li>
<li><strong>Limits.</strong> The free version may have a message limit; limits are shown in the app.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. User Content, community and moderation</h2>
<p>What you share in the community remains yours; we receive only the limited licence needed to operate the Service, and we take moderation decisions transparently in accordance with the EU Digital Services Act (DSA).</p>

<h3>8.1. Rights in content and licence</h3>
<ul>
